{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvo3nqnBdtEd6uLbJ8sd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing is set up here yet. The project's `.claude/skills` folder is empty, and I don't have any email-finder API connected. To get this you need two things.\n\n**1. A way to confirm who the CTO is right now.** Stripe's CTO has changed a few times recently. Rahul Patil held the role and then left for Anthropic in late 2025, and I don't know for certain who has it today. I can check with web search, which is already available, so you don't need to set anything up for this part.\n\n**2. An email-finder API key.** Pick one of these:\n\n- Hunter.io. Its Email Finder endpoint takes a domain plus first and last name and returns the email with a confidence score. The free tier gives 25 searches a month.\n- Apollo.io. Its people match endpoint works from a name and company and also returns the title, which helps confirm the person is still the CTO.\n- Prospeo or Findymail. Both are tuned for verified B2B emails and usually do better on large company domains.\n\nOnce you have a key, export it in your shell, for example `export HUNTER_API_KEY=...`. Or put it in `.claude/settings.local.json` under `env` so I can read it. I'll call the API with curl.\n\n**Optional but worth it: a verifier.** NeverBounce, ZeroBounce or MillionVerifier will check the result. Big domains like stripe.com are often \"accept-all,\" which means the mail server accepts any address and verification can't prove the mailbox exists. In that case you get a likely pattern, such as `firstname at stripe.com`, with a confidence score, not a confirmed address.\n\nWith the key in place, the flow is: I look up the current CTO, call the finder with their name and `stripe.com`, then verify the result. That's about three calls.\n\nA cold email to a named exec counts as B2B outreach under GDPR and CAN-SPAM. Include an opt-out and a legitimate business reason.\n\nWhich provider do you want to use? Once the key is set, I'll run the lookup."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":124,"cache_read_input_tokens":24945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":124},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba5ce52a-fcc1-4820-9fd5-89dcc9061b1e","uuid":"938c5337-025f-4049-9fca-89b2b8e8540c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T16:50:57.661Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvo3nWRfWRQDkVuEfXzv"}
